{"id":"07-prompting","number":7,"slug":"prompting-coding-agents","title":"Talking to agents","short":"Talking to agents","module":"Working with one agent","summary":"Good prompts aren't clever. They answer one question: how is the model supposed to know what I mean? Learn the habits of people who prompt agents all day: point to where knowledge lives, show a gold standard, state constraints and exit criteria, and use the short phrases that carry a lot of discipline.","voice":"Eric","scenes":[{"template":"title","chapter":"Intro","narration":"The best prompts for coding agents aren't clever. There are no magic words. They just answer one question better than most people bother to.","params":{"kicker":"Lesson 7","module":"Module 2 · Working with one agent","title":"Talking to *agents*","subtitle":"How is the model supposed to know what you mean?","bubble":"Tell me more…","mood":"happy"},"start":0.5,"dur":9.559,"words":[{"text":"The","s":0.8,"e":0.96},{"text":"best","s":1.12,"e":1.28},{"text":"prompts","s":1.4,"e":1.68},{"text":"for","s":1.76,"e":1.84},{"text":"coding","s":1.92,"e":2.16},{"text":"agents","s":2.24,"e":2.64},{"text":"aren't","s":2.72,"e":2.88},{"text":"clever.","s":2.96,"e":3.84},{"text":"There","s":3.92,"e":4},{"text":"are","s":4.08,"e":4.16},{"text":"no","s":4.24,"e":4.4},{"text":"magic","s":4.48,"e":4.8},{"text":"words.","s":4.88,"e":5.76},{"text":"They","s":5.84,"e":5.92},{"text":"just","s":6.04,"e":6.16},{"text":"answer","s":6.36,"e":6.56},{"text":"one","s":6.64,"e":6.8},{"text":"question","s":6.88,"e":7.36},{"text":"better","s":7.44,"e":7.6},{"text":"than","s":7.72,"e":7.84},{"text":"most","s":7.96,"e":8.08},{"text":"people","s":8.24,"e":8.4},{"text":"bother","s":8.44,"e":8.72},{"text":"to.","s":8.84,"e":9.2}]},{"template":"statement","chapter":"The kidnapped engineer","narration":"Thorsten Ball, who builds the Amp agent, uses this picture. Imagine a brilliant senior engineer, kidnapped and locked in a room, with only a computer and your note: fix t